From 1c0fe5af91ee893703de7e1d4b3b9de85559ec24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oxp3-fixes <oxp3-fixes@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:31:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/vrr: VRR over a DP-to-HDMI 2.1 PCON

Implement the TODOs in intel_vrr_is_capable() and intel_dp_needs_as_sdp()
for a DP-to-HDMI 2.1 protocol converter, the way amdgpu drives one. The
PCON converts the variable DP timing to HDMI VRR; the source:

- detects that the PCON takes the header-only Adaptive-Sync SDP v1;
- sends that packet whenever the mode is in the VRR range, at fixed and
  variable refresh alike, so the packet and the guardband it needs stay
  the same;
- sends the AMD FreeSync SPD InfoFrame (DP 1.3 InfoFrame SDP) next to
  that packet for an allow-listed PCON whose HDMI sink has an AMD
  FreeSync VSDB, with the range from that VSDB - amdgpu's
  FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_IN_WHITELIST packet set; its flags follow VRR;
- keeps the MSA VTotal at the mode's vtotal while VRR stretches frames
  ("MSA hold"). With VRR enabled the transcoder announces TRANS_VRR_VMAX
  as the MSA VTotal (converter-side capture: 2250 -> 6750 at 4K120 with
  a 40 Hz floor), and the Synaptics VMM6210 rebuilds its HDMI output
  from that value - a 40 Hz base timing, which gave duplicated rows,
  black and dock resets. With DC balance adjust enabled the timing
  generator takes its limits from the DCB VMAX/FLIPLINE registers, so on
  such an output (pipe A/B, display 30+) TRANS_VRR_VMAX stays at the
  vtotal and the real VMAX goes into the DCB registers; the DMC
  balancing loop stays off and the adjust counters stay 0. Readout takes
  VMAX from the DCB register while this is active;
- sets MSA timing ignore (DP_DOWNSPREAD_CTRL) after the video stream is
  running instead of during link training, as amdgpu does
  (enable_stream_features() after unblank) and as the Windows driver
  does (after its link-training loop);
- reads the header-only packet back (the readout accepted only v2's
  9-byte payload, which made the state checker fail);
- takes the VRR range from the HDMI Forum VSDB when the EDID has no
  EDID 1.4 range descriptor (common for TVs with EDID 1.3);
- sends YCbCr 4:2:0 straight through a PCON that can pass it, instead of
  YCbCr 4:4:4 for the PCON to convert (4K120 on a 2-lane HBR3 link still
  needs DSC either way: DP carries 4:2:0 at the full pixel rate);
- offers VRR on such an output; xe.pcon_vrr=0 turns it off;
- logs the SPD bytes the hardware holds on DP outputs during state
  readout ("DP SPD SDP readback:", drm.debug KMS), since the HDMI
  unpack can't decode the DP-packed packet: bytes 11-13 are 03 78 78 at
  fixed 120 Hz and 07 28 78 with VRR active on a 40-120 Hz sink.

Replaces the OneXPlayer 3 series 0010-0029 and 0201-0204 (one change
per test, a VRR range cap, 4:2:0 and MSA-ignore bisection switches)
with this single change. The Anatase 7.3.4-an02 tag already carries the
first of them ("drm/i915/vrr: allow VRR over a DP-to-HDMI 2.1 PCON");
this patch applies on top of it and supersedes it.

Hardware: OneXPlayer 3 (Panther Lake), JSAUX HB1201B USB-C dock with a
Synaptics VMM6210 PCON (OUI 90-cc-24, DPCD 0x007 = 0xc2: MSA timing
ignore supported; DPCD 0x2214 = 0x01: AS SDP, no FAVT), LG TV
"LG TV SSCR2" (HF-VSDB VRR 40-120 Hz).
